WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:02.869
Everyone, today I'm going to take you

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.371
to a really cool place where

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.806
you can recycle seven plastic bottles

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.141
and make a piece of clothing

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.376
. This is something that

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:11.111
netizens have been wanting us to film for a long time,

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.012
so today

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:14.247
we're serious about picking up the pieces

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.115
and showing everyone

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:16.750
the textile industry in Changhua.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:17.484
Let's On

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.353
the day of filming,

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.355
the factory machines were running at full capacity,

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.424
and the sounds of the machines provided the most authentic production atmosphere.

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:25.892
So, after filming, we decided to

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:26.793
return to the studio

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.461
to re-post-produce and re-dub the video

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:29.863
for everyone to see.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:30.397
Welcome to

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:31.231
Taiwan's Changhua

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.766
Textile Industry

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.434
. Taiwan's textile industry is truly impressive,

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.669
whether it's fabrics, functional fabrics,

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:37.637
sweatshirts

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:39.005
, or even all sorts of other

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.373
unusual clothing you can't imagine.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.175
Many of these fabrics are exported worldwide,

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:43.977
and today I'm going to tell you something

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:44.978
quite unique : how

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:46.813
you can make a brand new piece of clothing

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.982
out of seven plastic bottles.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.917
Do you know how impressive Taiwan's fabric making

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.886
is? I'm not talking about plastics,

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:54.521
of course, it can't

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:55.789
compare to Southeast Asia or mainland China

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.524
, but Taiwan's functional fabrics

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.793
hold over 50% of

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:00.760
the global market share.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:01.561
Wow, that's a lot!

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.395
Over 50%!

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.064
Taiwan

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.165
is truly impressive

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.232
in the field of functional fabrics , especially

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.802
for outdoor brands.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:10.470
Do you know what percentage Taiwan holds?

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.172
I'm talking about the entire world,

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:12.872
70% .

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:13.640
That's a lot!

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.607
70%. It's actually

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:15.675
quite impressive.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:16.676
You must find it hard to imagine, right?

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.411
In the past, we imagined

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.479
dyeing

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.481
or fabric manufacturing

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.550
as highly polluting and labor-intensive

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.985
, or family-run factories where

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.287
they slowly threaded

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:28.588
warp

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.757
and weft with a shuttle to weave fabric. Fabrics

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.625
without functionality are different.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.727
Taiwan is one of the few countries that's

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:37.230
quite advanced in polyester recycling and

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.098
fabric

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:39.365
research and development

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.334
. So today, let's start with a basic concept

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.235
: plastic bottles.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:44.003
Plastic bottles are called PET.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.972
People in the industry call it PET

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.941
. How many kL is your PET? Is your PET pure?

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:50.110
PET's scientific name in Chinese is

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:53.379
polyethylene terephthalate,

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:54.881
right? It's quite difficult,

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:55.315
the chemistry is quite difficult,

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:56.349
and

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.517
it's generally called PET.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:58.885
PET is

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:01.054
the most common material many of us use

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.222
when recycling plastic bottles.

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:03.723
But it's not the only thing that can be recycled.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.058
In fact, many things can be recycled . It's

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:06.226
just that the recycling of plastic bottles

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:07.393
is relatively mature

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.628
in the recycling industry

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.096
. So if you can imagine

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:11.564
more applications for recycling,

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:13.399
you can start small and grow up to make a fortune.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:15.034
So usually, after drinking beverages

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.302
or mineral water in plastic bottles,

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.271
we will throw them into the recycling room

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.073
or the resource recycling truck,

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.241
right? It goes through several steps

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.575
. The first is sorting,

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.911
because there are different numbers on the back.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:25.945
Then there are colors.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:26.980
Even PET

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.481
has different colors.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.116
After cleaning the bottle caps,

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:32.051
the first major step

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.987
is crushing.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.889
In fact, crushing is a very important step.

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.690
Basically, in all industrial production

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.359
and recycling mechanisms,

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:41.928
most people usually use crushing,

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:44.197
whether it's recycled metal or recycled materials.

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:45.632
When you want to

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.467
remelt and remake something,

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.202
we often use crushing.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.003
Otherwise, imagine

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.604
if you were to use plastic bottles to make clothes today,

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.273
would they look like this?

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:55.074
Plastic bottle clothes are difficult to move, right?

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.342
And they are very sharp, so no one will buy them.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.211
So usually we return them to

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:59.612
their original raw material

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.514
, PET. After RPET is crushed

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:02.815
, it will become small particles.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.984
When you pick it up with your hands, it will feel like this.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:07.120
These are actually

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.189
clean fragments that

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:10.156
have been selected.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:12.158
So, many 3C

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:14.160
products that are updated every year

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.828
can be

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.230
crushed and recycled in this way.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.765
But first of all, your material

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:20.266
must be pure and clean so that it will not

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.501
be contaminated by a lot of things

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:22.669
when it is crushed,

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:24.871
and it cannot be re-melted and re-made.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.039
This is a basic concept.

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.840
Of course, you can't start using it after it is crushed

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.275
. Usually, we still need to

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.910
clean it, pump out water, and dry it

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.812
, and then use a strong magnet

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.180
to absorb the impurities.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.815
But you must think that the strong magnet

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.050
is like using a magnet to absorb it.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.618
This is the principle of mechanical design.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.987
When you drop your crushed materials down, you can

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:43.590
see these small sticks on top.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.225
They actually have magnets inside.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:47.060
Because sometimes

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.728
people will stuff things into plastic bottles,

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.563
or they may be attached to them

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:51.898
, or when there are a lot of debris,

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.233
they may stick to them.

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:54.901
You can use a strong magnet in the middle

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.970
to absorb some impurities,

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.171
so that your material will be pure.

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.439
Then, basically,

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:01.107
when these materials are clean,

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:02.609
you can melt them.

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:04.277
Melting is actually a kind of heating.

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:05.878
Heat it to make it soft

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:06.713
so that it sticks together.

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:07.814
Have you ever eaten

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:08.781
Japanese flowing noodles?

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.550
It's like this flowing noodles.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.718
We will take the

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:13.386
melted PET

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:15.388
and turn it into noodles.

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:17.357
After melting, it becomes small noodles.

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:18.791
Next, we need to do another thing,

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:19.525
which is granulation.

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:20.960
Because the material is now clean

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:21.995
and becomes sticks.

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:23.229
Have you ever seen

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.464
people making candies as a child

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:25.565
and

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:26.933
then cutting it...

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:27.734
cutting it into pieces?

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.469
So granulation is actually the same thing.

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:30.970
Why do we cut it into pieces?

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.872
First, it is easier to store

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.073
because it

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.675
is not easy to roll noodles.

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:36.209
Then,

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:37.944
it can be sold as material to others

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:39.312
, or it

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:40.980
will be more convenient for the next step.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.249
Do you remember

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:45.151
when we were in India, we saw people injecting things?

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.486
We injected the helmets.

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:48.087
The material is actually one by one.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:49.022
In

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.089
the injection molding machine,

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:52.091
the granular raw materials

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.359
are usually the best to use.

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:54.327
So after that, you put

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:56.195
these particles into this small barrel.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:57.163
You think it is only this small,

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:57.930
but it is not.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:58.731
This is also

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.466
the entire copper barrel. The entire chimney

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.135
is filled with granulated particles.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.736
This is a large factory.

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:04.904
Next, these small particles

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.806
will enter the molten state again.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.308
The black things inside

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:09.142
are actually masterbatches

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:10.209
. The colors they emit

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.577
can be adjusted

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:12.712
with these different masterbatches

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:14.480
. Have you ever used a

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.648
shower head at home?

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:16.449
You can imagine that

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:17.917
it has melted and

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:19.452
turned into a liquid.

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:21.988
Then, when it comes out of your shower head,

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:24.424
it will spray out like a shower.

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:25.191
The concept

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:26.726
is that the motors on it will

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:27.794
squeeze out these molten particles

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:29.429
through pressure ,

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:31.030
and it will not break.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.332
It is like a line,

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:33.566
so it is divided into

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:35.535
12, 36, and 72 strands, which

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:37.103
are all kinds of different strands

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:38.471
, but in the end it becomes

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:40.340
You must be wondering what this strand is, right? When

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.575
we describe fibers, we usually

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:43.409
say this.

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:44.544
Look, this is a line, right?

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:46.045
But if you look at the end of the line,

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.513
it is divided into

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:48.881
many strands...

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:50.983
When we talk about making textiles and fibers,

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:52.452
we call this a strand.

00:05:52.452 --> 00:05:55.154
Now you have the concept of a strand and a line, right?

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.956
So, then you have to enter

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:57.957
the automatic doffing machine.

00:05:57.957 --> 00:05:59.359
The automatic doffing machine is

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:00.460
to divide these materials,

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:01.427
the original plastic bottles,

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:02.628
the original small particles,

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:04.964
and the strands after being melted

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:06.265
into strands again,

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:08.301
and finally become a line.

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:09.602
How do

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.070
you collect this line? After collecting it

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.238
, it is rolled into a roll.

00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:13.306
That's it. A roll of thread.

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:15.508
So now you see humans making a thread.

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:18.010
No matter if you watch wilderness survival channels,

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.045
you will see people

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:20.346
taking plant vines

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:21.080
, stripping them into silk

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.148
, and then rolling them up like this.

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:23.483
It is actually the same concept, which

00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:24.484
is to weave different strands

00:06:24.484 --> 00:06:26.018
into a thread

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:27.720
to make it a strong thread.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.322
So after the previous steps,

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:30.857
you will make two kinds of threads.

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:31.758
You can think of them as

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:33.059
finished products and semi-finished

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:33.793
products. The so-called finished product

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:35.128
means that it can be used directly,

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:36.596
for example, it can be used to make some

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:37.497
blackout cloth,

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:38.231
windbreakers,

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:39.899
and some fabrics for outdoor products.

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:41.167
The other semi-finished product

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:43.002
means that it needs to be processed again

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:44.270
. The two threads

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:45.772
look different.

00:06:45.772 --> 00:06:46.773
One is loose and

00:06:46.773 --> 00:06:48.174
the other is like noodles. No,

00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:48.908
the two are different.

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:49.509
This one, which

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:51.277
has not been false-twisted

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:52.545
, is called a semi-finished product.

00:06:52.545 --> 00:06:53.446
So you see, although its lines

00:06:53.446 --> 00:06:54.781
look shiny

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:55.882
, when I pull them,

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:57.550
they actually have no tension

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:58.851
. When I tighten it and then pull it,

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:00.720
there is no tension and no elasticity.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.089
But the other line that has been false-twisted,

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:04.624
you see, I tighten it as well.

00:07:04.624 --> 00:07:05.992
Do you find

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:07.527
that it feels

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:08.628
like a shock absorber?

00:07:08.628 --> 00:07:10.563
It looks very fluffy, like permed hair, just like

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.432
when you were a kid, did you use corn silk

00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:13.499
to curl your hair?

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:14.867
After curling, it will have elasticity,

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:16.202
so your clothes

00:07:16.202 --> 00:07:18.004
will be comfortable to wear and will become fluffy.

00:07:18.004 --> 00:07:19.172
So, think about

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:21.441
something hard like a plastic bottle.

00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:22.942
Once it is false-twisted, The correct processing

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:24.377
makes it still very fluffy when worn.

00:07:24.377 --> 00:07:26.112
What is the concept of false twist? I tell you

00:07:26.112 --> 00:07:28.014
, you are lucky to meet me today.

00:07:28.014 --> 00:07:30.349
The concept of false twist is that you can imagine that

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:31.384
this is a thread.

00:07:31.384 --> 00:07:33.986
False twist means turning it in the clockwise direction

00:07:33.986 --> 00:07:35.955
and the counter-clockwise direction.

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.623
After turning it like this,

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:39.091
it becomes tight, right?

00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:41.461
After it is tightened, turn

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:42.395
it back and it becomes fluffy,

00:07:42.395 --> 00:07:43.830
but it is still the same.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.898
Its inner bones

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:47.233
have been sorted out, you know.

00:07:47.233 --> 00:07:49.268
And the false twist machine room is very spectacular.

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:50.570
It grows like this

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.505
, and the whole picture you see now

00:07:52.505 --> 00:07:54.607
is actually like a cycle

00:07:54.607 --> 00:07:56.275
. It starts from this side

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:59.145
and goes up,

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:01.147
then goes down,

00:08:01.147 --> 00:08:02.081
and then goes back

00:08:02.081 --> 00:08:03.683
to become the bundle of threads

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:04.984
you see now

00:08:04.984 --> 00:08:06.252
. Why does it have to run a full circle

00:08:06.252 --> 00:08:08.588
? In fact, the most critical part is this needle.

00:08:08.588 --> 00:08:10.556
This needle basically rotates tens of thousands of times per minute

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:11.891
, and it spins

00:08:11.891 --> 00:08:14.327
like crazy like this ,

00:08:14.327 --> 00:08:16.729
and then twists your thread again.

00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:17.830
And you see this other area

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:18.965
of ​​shiny yarn.

00:08:18.965 --> 00:08:21.200
This is the wedding veil that you girls want to wear

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.636
when you get married.

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:24.737
Why does the wedding veil look

00:08:24.737 --> 00:08:25.805
so shiny? It is because it

00:08:25.805 --> 00:08:27.874
has been processed into shiny yarn

00:08:27.874 --> 00:08:30.643
during the production process.

00:08:30.643 --> 00:08:32.845
So you see, it looks very cool under the light

00:08:32.845 --> 00:08:35.047
. So when you wear clothes normally,

00:08:35.047 --> 00:08:36.282
you will not think about

00:08:36.282 --> 00:08:37.583
the huge equipment behind it

00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:39.418
, which helps you weave the threads one by one

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:40.686
, and finally it becomes clothes

00:08:40.686 --> 00:08:42.221
, but it is still far from being clothes

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:43.856
because After finishing this step,

00:08:43.856 --> 00:08:45.591
they actually have to go to the most serious,

00:08:45.591 --> 00:08:47.293
tragic and cruel place

00:08:47.293 --> 00:08:48.060
, which is QC. QC

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.695
is not done after the clothes are finished,

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:51.864
but QC is done on the online part. Because I produce

00:08:51.864 --> 00:08:53.566
thousands or tens of thousands of

00:08:53.566 --> 00:08:55.067
thread bundles at a time

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:56.135
before they are slowly woven into cloth, and

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:58.037
the cloth is counted in batches and bundles,

00:08:58.037 --> 00:08:59.505
so they will weave these threads

00:08:59.505 --> 00:09:01.240
into the shape of a sock,

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:03.142
very similar to the socks with pullovers,

00:09:03.142 --> 00:09:04.043
and then go into the dyeing room

00:09:04.043 --> 00:09:05.578
to be dyed into a special color.

00:09:05.578 --> 00:09:06.379
Then you see,

00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:07.880
when you pass it through the sock,

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.348
you will see different color levels,

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:10.483
right? It looks a little different.

00:09:10.483 --> 00:09:11.517
If it looks different,

00:09:11.517 --> 00:09:12.518
then all of them will be rejected

00:09:12.518 --> 00:09:14.053
because if they send it abroad

00:09:14.053 --> 00:09:15.688
and find that the color level is too different

00:09:15.688 --> 00:09:17.790
or if it is sent to If the quality is not good abroad,

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.091
not just the bundle will be picked out,

00:09:19.091 --> 00:09:20.893
but the entire container will be returned. It's

00:09:20.893 --> 00:09:21.761
terrible, and

00:09:21.761 --> 00:09:23.062
you even have to pay for the shipping fee yourself.

00:09:23.062 --> 00:09:24.463
Okay, now

00:09:24.463 --> 00:09:25.965
you know how to make the thread

00:09:25.965 --> 00:09:28.200
, but it's still a long way

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:29.068
from making your clothes or your piece of cloth.

00:09:29.068 --> 00:09:30.903
First of all, you have to understand the longitude and latitude.

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:32.238
Have you heard of longitude

00:09:32.238 --> 00:09:33.105
and latitude ?

00:09:33.105 --> 00:09:33.973
The longitude and latitude

00:09:33.973 --> 00:09:34.907
of the earth.

00:09:34.907 --> 00:09:36.742
In fact, when we talk about cloth, we will talk about the longitude and latitude.

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:38.210
So when you start to make a piece of cloth,

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:39.712
you have to go through the warping. The warping

00:09:51.691 --> 00:09:52.625
is very spectacular

00:09:52.625 --> 00:09:55.127
. You take the bundles of thread you just made

00:09:55.127 --> 00:09:56.495
, and then you arrange them neatly

00:09:56.495 --> 00:09:57.597
into a line array,

00:09:57.597 --> 00:09:58.664
just like this.

00:09:58.664 --> 00:09:59.732
Have

00:09:59.732 --> 00:10:00.533
you seen Dongfang Bubai? Do you know Dongfang Bubai?

00:10:00.533 --> 00:10:01.100
I don't know

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:02.268
if it's from your era.

00:10:02.268 --> 00:10:03.069
What is

00:10:03.069 --> 00:10:04.570
Dongfang Bubai? It's about thread.

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:06.005
Snap, a whole row of threads.

00:10:06.439 --> 00:10:07.340
No one knows.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:08.708
Haven't you read Jin Yong?

00:10:08.708 --> 00:10:09.909
People nowadays don't read Jin Yong.

00:10:09.909 --> 00:10:10.876
Anyway, there is a person

00:10:10.876 --> 00:10:12.411
whose trick is to shoot out a thread array

00:10:12.812 --> 00:10:13.980
like warping . The key

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:15.514
is to control the tension of each thread very well

00:10:15.514 --> 00:10:17.750
when pulling out the thread array.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.418
That is the adjustment of the machine

00:10:19.418 --> 00:10:20.753
. If the tension is not pulled well

00:10:20.753 --> 00:10:22.021
, then when you are weaving,

00:10:22.021 --> 00:10:23.656
you will see that the cloth is crooked,

00:10:23.656 --> 00:10:24.991
or it will break easily.

00:10:24.991 --> 00:10:26.892
This is very subtle but very important.

00:10:26.892 --> 00:10:27.960
But usually no one knows.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:29.595
After the threads are arranged,

00:10:29.595 --> 00:10:30.930
we have to go through a step

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:31.897
called sizing

00:10:31.897 --> 00:10:34.033
. Sizing can be imagined as sizing clothes.

00:10:34.033 --> 00:10:35.201
There are many kinds of sizing materials

00:10:35.201 --> 00:10:36.902
. In the old days, people called it white glue

00:10:36.902 --> 00:10:38.671
, or they can put some

00:10:38.671 --> 00:10:40.706
coatings on your threads.

00:10:40.706 --> 00:10:42.575
So you When you first get the clothes,

00:10:42.575 --> 00:10:44.410
do you feel that they are very stiff? The clothes are very stiff

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:46.212
and look a little shiny .

00:10:46.212 --> 00:10:48.214
After a few washes in the washing machine,

00:10:48.214 --> 00:10:49.882
your clothes will become more and more worn and wrinkled.

00:10:49.882 --> 00:10:51.283
In fact, one benefit of starching

00:10:51.283 --> 00:10:53.085
is that it can increase the friction of the clothes

00:10:53.085 --> 00:10:54.220
and make them more durable.

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:55.588
Therefore, starching is usually used

00:10:55.588 --> 00:10:56.756
. Next, your PET bottle fabric

00:10:56.756 --> 00:10:57.957
has been processed to 50%.

00:10:57.957 --> 00:10:59.225
After this step,

00:10:59.225 --> 00:11:01.027
we will proceed to

00:11:01.027 --> 00:11:02.561
warp stitching. You have the concept of warp. Then

00:11:02.561 --> 00:11:04.430
, warp stitching is to stitch two different warp threads

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.331
together.

00:11:05.331 --> 00:11:06.732
Sometimes its purpose is to match

00:11:06.732 --> 00:11:07.633
colors

00:11:07.633 --> 00:11:08.901
, make the clothes have layers,

00:11:08.901 --> 00:11:10.569
or color or pattern.

00:11:10.569 --> 00:11:12.304
It will go through the warp stitching action.

00:11:12.304 --> 00:11:13.639
Next, the next action is

00:11:13.639 --> 00:11:14.874
It needs to be divided into upper and lower layers

00:11:14.874 --> 00:11:15.741
, which is called Lingqu.

00:11:23.315 --> 00:11:24.250
Why Lingqu?

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:25.918
It is to make it easier to weave in the heddle.

00:11:25.918 --> 00:11:26.952
Why weave

00:11:26.952 --> 00:11:28.854
in the heddle? Weaving in the heddle is to allow your cloth

00:11:28.854 --> 00:11:31.357
to find the front part of your front.

00:11:31.357 --> 00:11:32.758
At this time,

00:11:32.758 --> 00:11:35.961
you can decide whether your cloth

00:11:35.961 --> 00:11:37.630
should be plain woven, twill, or patterned. You

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:38.431
have to make a decision

00:11:38.431 --> 00:11:40.232
at this step. Then, according to

00:11:40.232 --> 00:11:41.534
the pattern designed for each cloth,

00:11:41.534 --> 00:11:42.735
each warp yarn will

00:11:42.735 --> 00:11:45.671
be inserted into the needle eye in the reed and heddle. It

00:11:45.671 --> 00:11:46.372
is very complicated, isn't it?

00:11:46.372 --> 00:11:49.008
It is unexpected that from the loom cloth farmers

00:11:49.008 --> 00:11:50.376
to the present, weaving has

00:11:50.376 --> 00:11:51.677
developed to its current state.

00:11:51.677 --> 00:11:52.611
So you can see

00:11:52.611 --> 00:11:53.946
why some people's

00:11:53.946 --> 00:11:55.648
cloth itself has different patterns,

00:11:55.648 --> 00:11:57.516
different colors, and different layers

00:11:57.516 --> 00:11:58.684
or Some functional fabrics

00:11:58.684 --> 00:12:01.454
will have features such as breathable inside, heat dissipation outside, and

00:12:01.454 --> 00:12:03.155
sweat absorption inside.

00:12:03.155 --> 00:12:04.256
After going through

00:12:04.256 --> 00:12:05.458
all these steps,

00:12:05.458 --> 00:12:06.592
you will be able to make

00:12:06.592 --> 00:12:08.627
the fabric and clothing style

00:12:08.627 --> 00:12:09.762
you have designed in your mind.

00:12:09.762 --> 00:12:10.863
Next, we will start weaving. When you

00:12:10.863 --> 00:12:12.131
were a child, have you ever heard the Three Character

00:12:12.131 --> 00:12:13.165
Classic? Human nature is inherently

00:12:13.165 --> 00:12:14.667
good, and natures are similar. Habits

00:12:14.667 --> 00:12:16.335
tend to separate us, etc. But the most important part is "If

00:12:16.335 --> 00:12:17.636
a child does not learn, he will break the loom."

00:12:17.636 --> 00:12:18.704
Do you know

00:12:18.704 --> 00:12:20.206
who the person who breaks the loom

00:12:20.206 --> 00:12:22.007
in the Three Character Classic

00:12:22.007 --> 00:12:23.209
is? It is Mencius' mother, Meng Mu.

00:12:23.209 --> 00:12:24.176
So how serious is breaking the loom

00:12:24.176 --> 00:12:25.377
? When we have just gone through

00:12:25.377 --> 00:12:26.779
so many steps,

00:12:26.779 --> 00:12:28.814
Meng Mu suddenly appeared in this factory.

00:12:29.582 --> 00:12:31.684
So how do you cut all

00:12:31.684 --> 00:12:33.886
the warp threads you have just arranged ?

00:12:33.886 --> 00:12:35.287
How serious is it? This is too

00:12:35.287 --> 00:12:35.988
serious

00:12:35.988 --> 00:12:37.289
.

00:12:37.289 --> 00:12:39.125
This is what the ancients called "breaking the shuttle."

00:12:39.125 --> 00:12:40.059
I always thought that breaking the shuttle

00:12:40.059 --> 00:12:41.861
meant breaking the machine,

00:12:41.861 --> 00:12:42.361
not the machine.

00:12:42.361 --> 00:12:43.062
Although you know,

00:12:43.062 --> 00:12:45.131
in the past, Chinese teachers talked about breaking the shuttle

00:12:45.131 --> 00:12:46.799
. The shuttle is actually the shuttle.

00:12:46.799 --> 00:12:49.034
We just said that it is the straight warp.

00:12:49.034 --> 00:12:50.202
Then we tie a weft on

00:12:50.202 --> 00:12:51.737
the shuttle

00:12:51.737 --> 00:12:52.838
and pass it through.

00:12:52.838 --> 00:12:54.673
Then you will take something that looks like a ruler.

00:12:55.841 --> 00:12:57.276
So in the past, people said breaking the shuttle

00:12:57.276 --> 00:12:59.044
means breaking the shuttle.

00:12:59.044 --> 00:13:00.212
The Chinese meaning is like this,

00:13:00.212 --> 00:13:01.947
but I tell you, when I was learning to weave,

00:13:01.947 --> 00:13:03.449
the teacher didn't mean it.

00:13:03.449 --> 00:13:04.116
The breaking the shuttle is like

00:13:04.116 --> 00:13:05.351
in many cartoons.

00:13:05.351 --> 00:13:07.153
Meng Mu cuts the warp

00:13:07.153 --> 00:13:08.287
.

00:13:08.287 --> 00:13:09.789
If the warp is cut,

00:13:09.789 --> 00:13:11.557
the whole piece of cloth is useless

00:13:11.557 --> 00:13:13.692
because you break the shuttle. The cloth can still be used.

00:13:13.692 --> 00:13:15.261
She can warp it once. No,

00:13:15.261 --> 00:13:16.395
it can't be warped

00:13:16.395 --> 00:13:17.797
because warping means you

00:13:17.797 --> 00:13:19.765
warp it straight like this, back and forth once.

00:13:19.765 --> 00:13:21.700
If it breaks, there's no way to straighten it back again, which is

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:22.768
a waste of work

00:13:22.768 --> 00:13:24.837
. So, actually, my Chinese teacher

00:13:24.837 --> 00:13:26.572
and my weaving teacher

00:13:26.572 --> 00:13:28.307
said two completely different versions.

00:13:28.307 --> 00:13:30.976
Usually, according to industrial production,

00:13:30.976 --> 00:13:33.379
I believe the version the weaving teacher said

00:13:33.379 --> 00:13:34.513
, which is to cut the warp.

00:13:34.513 --> 00:13:36.115
But the key is that

00:13:36.115 --> 00:13:37.716
you have to learn it well, otherwise I will be angry.

00:13:37.716 --> 00:13:39.018
No matter in industrial production,

00:13:39.018 --> 00:13:40.052
if she wants to go all out,

00:13:40.052 --> 00:13:41.453
she will definitely cut the warp.

00:13:41.453 --> 00:13:43.122
That's how I let my son know that

00:13:43.122 --> 00:13:44.390
your grandmother shouldn't do it anymore.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:46.559
It's up for discussion. There are official history and unofficial history.

00:13:46.559 --> 00:13:48.327
So now we have straight lines,

00:13:48.327 --> 00:13:49.395
but a piece of clothing

00:13:49.395 --> 00:13:50.696
doesn't only have Straight lines,

00:13:50.696 --> 00:13:51.864
so at this time you need to use the weft

00:13:51.864 --> 00:13:53.899
and weave it horizontally into a piece of cloth

00:13:53.899 --> 00:13:56.268
, just weave it into cloth like this,

00:13:56.268 --> 00:13:57.436
it's not like this

00:13:57.436 --> 00:13:59.939
, so at this time the warp and weft come in,

00:13:59.939 --> 00:14:01.373
we need to enter the weft part.

00:14:06.946 --> 00:14:08.581
There are actually two

00:14:08.581 --> 00:14:09.415
ways to transmit the weft.

00:14:09.415 --> 00:14:10.916
One of them was to use water

00:14:10.916 --> 00:14:12.184
to shoot it with water,

00:14:12.184 --> 00:14:13.152
just like Blastoise,

00:14:13.152 --> 00:14:13.919
just

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.289
use the power of water to shoot your weft

00:14:17.289 --> 00:14:17.890
through,

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:19.358
and then the one that bounces back in the middle

00:14:19.358 --> 00:14:20.292
is called a heddle.

00:14:20.292 --> 00:14:20.993
Imagine that

00:14:20.993 --> 00:14:22.428
I have a straight warp

00:14:22.428 --> 00:14:23.829
in front of me, and

00:14:23.829 --> 00:14:26.065
now when the weft passes through,

00:14:26.065 --> 00:14:27.533
I need a heddle

00:14:27.533 --> 00:14:29.001
to bring it back,

00:14:29.001 --> 00:14:30.369
otherwise the line will be scattered in the middle,

00:14:30.369 --> 00:14:32.338
so Blastoise shoots once

00:14:32.338 --> 00:14:33.472
and then bounces back once.

00:14:33.472 --> 00:14:34.607
Shoot once, hit back once

00:14:34.607 --> 00:14:35.641
, shoot once, hit back once.

00:14:35.641 --> 00:14:37.509
In the past, with traditional looms,

00:14:37.509 --> 00:14:39.411
we would take a shuttle

00:14:39.411 --> 00:14:41.280
and throw it

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:42.581
forward.

00:14:42.581 --> 00:14:44.283
Whoosh, whoosh, whoosh, whoosh .

00:14:44.283 --> 00:14:45.951
Now, because of the advancement of air compressors

00:14:45.951 --> 00:14:46.986
and our

00:14:46.986 --> 00:14:48.787
precision pneumatic components

00:14:48.787 --> 00:14:50.122
, we can now use air jets

00:14:50.122 --> 00:14:52.258
to thread the needle. Just like that, puff, puff, puff. Finally,

00:14:52.258 --> 00:14:56.195
after the warp and weft are interwoven on both sides,

00:14:56.195 --> 00:14:59.164
the piece of cloth woven by the Cowherd and the Weaver Girl

00:14:59.164 --> 00:15:00.966
is finally completed

00:15:00.966 --> 00:15:02.601
. Did you know that the Weaver Girl weaves cloth?

00:15:02.601 --> 00:15:03.302
Nonsense

00:15:03.302 --> 00:15:04.303
, did you know that

00:15:04.303 --> 00:15:06.605
the Cowherd sells cattle? The Cowherd chops trees .

00:15:06.605 --> 00:15:08.607
How could it be that the Cowherd doesn't chop trees ?

00:15:08.607 --> 00:15:10.209
The Cowherd doesn't chop trees. The Cowherd herds cattle.

00:15:10.209 --> 00:15:10.542
Then who

00:15:10.542 --> 00:15:11.911
chops trees

00:15:11.911 --> 00:15:12.378
?

00:15:12.378 --> 00:15:13.646
Wu Gang,

00:15:13.646 --> 00:15:15.247
Wu Gang chops trees, right?

00:15:15.481 --> 00:15:16.448
So, look at that.

00:15:16.448 --> 00:15:18.117
A piece of clothing is just like that.

00:15:18.117 --> 00:15:20.119
What you think is a small recycling process

00:15:20.119 --> 00:15:21.820
is actually happening behind the scenes

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:22.955
in the invisible factory.

00:15:22.955 --> 00:15:25.090
There is a huge production chain

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:26.191
that helps you recycle

00:15:26.191 --> 00:15:27.459
and reuse it.

00:15:27.459 --> 00:15:29.128
So when you see some clothes marked

00:15:29.128 --> 00:15:31.063
as made of recycled polyester,

00:15:31.063 --> 00:15:32.898
there are actually many

00:15:32.898 --> 00:15:34.166
mechanical engineers

00:15:34.166 --> 00:15:35.668
, equipment manufacturers,

00:15:35.668 --> 00:15:37.736
and R&amp;D people who

00:15:37.736 --> 00:15:39.538
have tried every possible way to improve

00:15:39.538 --> 00:15:40.873
the traditional

00:15:40.873 --> 00:15:41.674
weaving process

00:15:41.674 --> 00:15:42.474
into this

00:15:42.474 --> 00:15:43.943
huge Taiwanese weaving industry. It

00:15:43.943 --> 00:15:45.210
is very great and powerful.

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:46.378
But why do we do this?

00:15:46.378 --> 00:15:47.546
Because the cost of doing this

00:15:47.546 --> 00:15:48.647
is relatively high.

00:15:48.647 --> 00:15:50.382
In fact, it is all to get rid of

00:15:50.382 --> 00:15:52.351
petrochemicals. The demand of the production chain,

00:15:52.351 --> 00:15:53.385
like the factory we filmed

00:15:53.385 --> 00:15:54.653
, actually helps

00:15:54.653 --> 00:15:56.488
a lot of very large

00:15:56.488 --> 00:15:58.791
production chains that everyone has at their disposal

00:15:58.791 --> 00:16:01.560
to supply their products and fabrics.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:03.696
Therefore, these very large companies

00:16:03.696 --> 00:16:05.764
will stipulate that your production process and your

00:16:05.764 --> 00:16:06.632
factory

00:16:06.632 --> 00:16:08.834
must have recycled machines

00:16:08.834 --> 00:16:09.768
ESG

00:16:09.768 --> 00:16:12.504
in order to supply

00:16:12.504 --> 00:16:14.606
all the product lines and materials of

00:16:14.606 --> 00:16:16.175
their company and brand. Although

00:16:16.175 --> 00:16:18.310
many of the scenes and factory equipment in our video today

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:20.679
are generally inaccessible,

00:16:20.679 --> 00:16:22.681
you still think these devices are very cool

00:16:22.681 --> 00:16:24.583
